            B.q("sa-m5-19", "sa-relational", "A steady production Azure SQL database will run at the same size for three years. How do you lower its compute cost the most?", listOf("Buy reserved capacity for three years in the vCore model", "Move it to the serverless tier with auto-pause after an hour", "Move it to the DTU Premium tier for a fixed monthly price", "Turn on read scale-out to use the replica at no extra charge"), setOf(0), "Azure SQL reserved capacity gives a discount on vCore compute for a one- or three-year commitment. It suits databases that run steadily at a known size.",
                scenario = "Saltway Rail's ticketing database behind its Android app runs at 16 vCores day and night, and its size has not changed in two years.",
                whyWrong = mapOf(
