            B.q("sa-m5-20", "sa-relational", "Customer support must see what a customer's address was on any past date, and the history must be kept by the database automatically. What do you recommend?", listOf("System-versioned temporal tables", "Dynamic data masking", "A nightly copy of the table", "Point-in-time restore each time someone asks"), setOf(0), "A system-versioned temporal table keeps every earlier version of each row in a history table, with the times it was valid. A query with FOR SYSTEM_TIME AS OF returns the data as it was on a date.",
